WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:02.080
- Hey guys, my name is Heinrich.

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:04.480
Welcome back to my
channel "Firm Learning",

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:06.860
and to another coffee break with me.

00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:09.560
It is actually the first coffee
that I was drinking today.

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:12.000
This morning I worked a lot in PowerPoint

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.130
on creating different types
of PowerPoint presentations

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:17.130
for the work that I'm currently doing,

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:20.661
and this just reminded me
of the time in consulting

00:00:20.661 --> 00:00:24.620
where I literally created
thousands of PowerPoint pages

00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:27.270
over a time span of about six years.

00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:30.060
I know that this can actually
be quite challenging.

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:32.230
It is quite a learning
development that you do

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:35.470
as a junior business
analyst joining consulting,

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:37.920
just learning the tools of PowerPoint

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:40.230
until you're a professional
of several years

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:42.700
and then really do these slides well.

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:44.560
There's much more to it than it seems.

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:46.050
Creating good and compelling

00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:49.120
PowerPoint presentations
is not easy at all,

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:51.390
it's really a craft that
you learn over time.

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:53.970
And even after one or
two years in consulting,

00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:56.690
you will still not be
there where you need to be

00:00:56.690 --> 00:00:59.220
to really have these things
at a professional level

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:01.730
where they need to be in the end.

00:01:01.730 --> 00:01:05.030
For that, I at some point a
few years ago created a course,

00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:07.680
it's called, "A Course on Slide Writing",

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:09.460
on creating PowerPoint presentations

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:11.600
as top consulting firms do.

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:13.900
And one of the topics that
I cover in this course

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:15.810
is action titles.

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:17.980
Action titles is an important part

00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:20.640
of every good professional
PowerPoint page.

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:24.310
It's the title that appears
in the very top of the page.

00:01:24.310 --> 00:01:27.260
And in this video, I would
like to give you an insight

00:01:27.260 --> 00:01:30.590
into how these action titles
are supposed to be written,

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:32.420
are supposed to be crafted.

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:34.850
And if you now say, "Who
cares about the title,

00:01:34.850 --> 00:01:37.860
"this is unimportant,"
you're completely wrong.

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:41.110
I can tell you, those action
titles are a crucial part

00:01:41.110 --> 00:01:43.230
of every PowerPoint presentation.

00:01:43.230 --> 00:01:45.320
So let me show you what's all about it

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:49.450
and how to write a good and
compelling action title.

00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:51.783
This section is all about action titles.

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:54.870
You already learned about action titles

00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:57.870
in the introductory section on storylines,

00:01:57.870 --> 00:01:59.650
but I think it is
important that you really

00:01:59.650 --> 00:02:01.620
understand this concept in detail,

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:03.300
because writing good action titles

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:07.280
is actually really important,
and very crucial and key

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:11.070
to create a winning and
successful storyline.

00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:13.580
So let's dive into a bit more detail.

00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:16.510
And what I have here is an
attempt of a definition.

00:02:16.510 --> 00:02:19.560
So this is my own very
personal definition.

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:21.160
Please don't cite me on that.

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:22.850
But I hope this helps you understand this

00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:24.400
a bit better what it is.

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:26.400
So let me just read it out to you.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:30.030
Action titles are headers
of a slide presentation

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:32.690
that summarize the content of the slide

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:35.053
by formulating a complete sentence.

00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:40.980
So, just to go in it point by
point what exactly that means.

00:02:41.470 --> 00:02:44.750
Action titles are the
headers of a presentation.

00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:46.410
So, the header would
be something like this.

00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:48.580
Here again, you see
that this is formulated

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:50.910
in the style of an action title.

00:02:50.910 --> 00:02:53.240
And then second, of a slide presentation.

00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:56.500
So yes, we are talking
about slide presentations

00:02:56.500 --> 00:02:58.780
like in PowerPoint or other programs.

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:01.310
So this is where action titles are used.

00:03:01.310 --> 00:03:05.240
And they're supposed to
summarize the content.

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:07.350
Here again, here's the definition,

00:03:07.350 --> 00:03:09.090
and then in the title, you always try

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:13.060
to really get the gist of
what the page is showing.

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:15.500
If you remember at the
beginning, there was the slide

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:17.910
with the horizontal
and the vertical logic.

00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:20.580
So, in order for you to
really write a winning logic,

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:22.380
you need to make sure
that the action titles

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:24.200
actually really represent

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:27.060
what the reader is seeing on the page.

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:29.360
And then finally, they are written

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:32.160
by formulating a complete sentence.

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:34.570
So if you look at these
titles, a title like that,

00:03:34.570 --> 00:03:36.750
you can see that it's
really a complete sentence,

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:38.480
so they had to create a clear storyline

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:40.090
within a presentation.

00:03:40.090 --> 00:03:43.050
It is not just the title
of a couple of words.

00:03:43.050 --> 00:03:45.470
You see these people
making quite often that,

00:03:45.470 --> 00:03:47.100
for instance on a slide like that,

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:48.780
somebody would only write

00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:51.790
action title definition
or something like that.

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:52.980
And the problem with that is that,

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:55.350
if you create the headers of your page

00:03:55.350 --> 00:03:58.130
or of your slide like that,
it's not really possible

00:03:58.130 --> 00:04:01.810
to just skip through all the
pages and get the key message.

00:04:01.810 --> 00:04:03.950
Because in most cases the titles,

00:04:03.950 --> 00:04:05.970
if you formulate them that way,

00:04:05.970 --> 00:04:08.470
won't really be speaking for themselves.

00:04:08.470 --> 00:04:12.260
It's usually then always
necessary to really read the page

00:04:12.260 --> 00:04:15.000
in order to get the key
message out of the page.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:18.730
But with action titles, we
want to enable exactly that,

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:22.410
so that the page itself
isn't that important anymore.

00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:25.013
The key message is already
in the action title.

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:32.270
And now I would like to
introduce a very familiar concept

00:04:32.270 --> 00:04:35.290
that can be helpful when
formulating action titles.

00:04:35.290 --> 00:04:38.690
So, if you struggle to come
up with the good action title,

00:04:38.690 --> 00:04:40.370
the reason for that
could be that your page

00:04:40.370 --> 00:04:44.087
actually lacks something
that is called a "So what?"

00:04:45.030 --> 00:04:47.950
So, what do we mean when we
talk about the "So what?"

00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:49.950
So, imagine you look at the slide,

00:04:49.950 --> 00:04:53.050
and there could be all kinds
of information on the slide.

00:04:53.050 --> 00:04:54.690
Maybe you did a fancy analysis,

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:57.800
you see different kinds
of charts and so on,

00:04:57.800 --> 00:05:00.360
and maybe that's interesting.

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:03.300
But sometimes you will find yourself

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:05.320
asking the question, so what?

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:07.940
So why does it matter
what I see on the slide?

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:11.550
What is the implication for my business,

00:05:11.550 --> 00:05:14.940
for the project that I'm working on?

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:17.730
That is depicted here on this slide.

00:05:17.730 --> 00:05:20.100
And this is actually what
many people do wrong.

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:22.430
They create some kind of analysis,

00:05:22.430 --> 00:05:25.150
and maybe it's fancy and
maybe it's interesting,

00:05:25.150 --> 00:05:27.770
but they lack to really put out there

00:05:27.770 --> 00:05:29.643
what the implication of that is.

00:05:29.643 --> 00:05:32.520
Or you could say they do not really show

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:35.133
what the "So what" of the page is.

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:38.550
So, whenever you struggle and wonder,

00:05:38.550 --> 00:05:40.033
do I really need this page,

00:05:41.506 --> 00:05:44.300
or ask yourself what a
good action title would be,

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:46.350
maybe start with asking yourself,

00:05:46.350 --> 00:05:48.950
so what, why do I need this page?

00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:50.740
So, what is the message?

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:53.680
And if you cannot really
come up with a good so what,

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:58.590
then probably this page
lacks a strong key message,

00:05:58.590 --> 00:06:00.440
and then you would either, usually,

00:06:00.440 --> 00:06:02.090
need to take this page out,

00:06:02.090 --> 00:06:05.710
or you would need to
restructure it, to recreate it,

00:06:05.710 --> 00:06:08.520
for you to enable it
to have a key message.

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:10.900
So, if you can't come
up with an action title,

00:06:10.900 --> 00:06:14.093
ask yourself critically if
this so what is actually there.

00:06:15.390 --> 00:06:18.150
What I will do now is, I
will give you an exercise

00:06:18.150 --> 00:06:21.270
which I hope will help you to really

00:06:21.270 --> 00:06:23.380
distinguish good from bad action titles,

00:06:23.380 --> 00:06:25.593
and you will see that in the next section.

00:06:27.010 --> 00:06:29.530
In this section, I'm
doing an exercise with you

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:32.240
that will hopefully
help you to distinguish

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:34.250
good action titles from bad,

00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:36.730
or maybe not so good action titles.

00:06:36.730 --> 00:06:39.050
And what you see here is a page,

00:06:39.050 --> 00:06:43.310
and I deleted the action
title from the page.

00:06:43.310 --> 00:06:45.280
I mean, it's not important
that you understand

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:46.750
all the nitty-gritty details,

00:06:46.750 --> 00:06:49.580
but just to quickly give you the summary.

00:06:49.580 --> 00:06:52.090
You see here kind of two regions,

00:06:52.090 --> 00:06:54.540
North America the first column here,

00:06:54.540 --> 00:06:56.980
and the second column Asia Pacific,

00:06:56.980 --> 00:06:59.060
and then there is some
kind of quantification

00:06:59.060 --> 00:07:00.710
of the EBIT potential.

00:07:00.710 --> 00:07:03.950
So EBIT is kind of a term for the profit,

00:07:03.950 --> 00:07:05.600
the profit of a company.

00:07:05.600 --> 00:07:07.440
So here's basically a profit potential

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:10.793
if the company would decide
to enter these regions,

00:07:12.010 --> 00:07:13.280
and we showed that here.

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:17.630
And so, the first question that
I would like to ask you is,

00:07:17.630 --> 00:07:20.533
what would be a good
action title to that page?

00:07:21.550 --> 00:07:23.170
So, please now pause the video

00:07:23.170 --> 00:07:24.830
and take whatever time you need

00:07:24.830 --> 00:07:26.610
to come up with a suggestion,

00:07:26.610 --> 00:07:29.760
and then afterwards we will
discuss this suggestion.

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:31.130
So stop the video now,

00:07:31.130 --> 00:07:33.080
and then let's resume in a few seconds.

00:07:37.160 --> 00:07:38.810
Okay, now you have a suggestion,

00:07:38.810 --> 00:07:41.690
and maybe even write it
down if that helps you.

00:07:41.690 --> 00:07:44.600
Because this way, you cannot
really cheat yourself.

00:07:44.600 --> 00:07:47.440
And what we will do
now is, we will go over

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:50.810
a couple of other suggestions
that I prepared for you.

00:07:50.810 --> 00:07:53.160
And after each one we can ask ourselves,

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:55.670
is this a good action title or not?

00:07:55.670 --> 00:07:58.120
And here again, feel
free to pause the video

00:07:58.120 --> 00:08:00.680
after every action title suggestion

00:08:00.680 --> 00:08:02.390
that I will blend in now.

00:08:02.390 --> 00:08:05.550
And before then I tell you
what I think, ask yourself

00:08:07.590 --> 00:08:09.457
is this a good action title or not?

00:08:10.860 --> 00:08:12.710
Let's begin with the first suggestion,

00:08:12.710 --> 00:08:15.370
derived potentials for an expansion.

00:08:15.370 --> 00:08:20.370
So would this be a good
action title to this page?

00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:21.920
And again, pause the video

00:08:21.920 --> 00:08:23.870
if you need a second to think about it.

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:28.430
And so here, I would argue no,

00:08:28.430 --> 00:08:30.250
this is not a good action title. Why not?

00:08:30.250 --> 00:08:33.580
Because actually, it doesn't
really fit in the definition.

00:08:33.580 --> 00:08:37.420
And why not? Because basically,
it's not a full sentence.

00:08:37.420 --> 00:08:39.520
It doesn't really give you

00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:43.380
the key message of this page in the title.

00:08:43.380 --> 00:08:46.410
It just tells you that
this is a title that has

00:08:46.410 --> 00:08:50.330
something to do with derived
potentials for an expansion,

00:08:50.330 --> 00:08:54.040
but it doesn't really tell
you what the potential is.

00:08:54.040 --> 00:08:55.770
So is this something good or bad,

00:08:55.770 --> 00:08:58.340
is the potential positive or negative?

00:08:58.340 --> 00:09:00.620
So basically, to really
get the message out of it,

00:09:00.620 --> 00:09:02.430
you would really have to read the page.

00:09:02.430 --> 00:09:03.263
Otherwise, it's not possible.

00:09:03.263 --> 00:09:06.000
And this is the opposite
of what an action title

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:06.933
is supposed to do.

00:09:09.910 --> 00:09:12.030
So this is the second example.

00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:13.630
Let me read it out to you.

00:09:13.630 --> 00:09:15.820
Expansion to new geographies

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:18.483
creates a positive EBIT potential.

00:09:19.563 --> 00:09:21.563
Once again, pause the video if you like.

00:09:23.120 --> 00:09:25.173
So, is this a good action title or not?

00:09:26.690 --> 00:09:29.180
And here, I would argue
that it's too generic.

00:09:29.180 --> 00:09:31.680
So it's a bit better than
the first section title,

00:09:31.680 --> 00:09:34.370
because this actually is a full sentence,

00:09:34.370 --> 00:09:35.820
and it really conveys a message.

00:09:35.820 --> 00:09:40.110
It says to you that there
is a positive EBIT potential

00:09:40.110 --> 00:09:43.160
in tapping these new geographies,

00:09:43.160 --> 00:09:44.680
but it's still too generic.

00:09:44.680 --> 00:09:46.660
You can get much more detailed than that,

00:09:46.660 --> 00:09:48.853
and we will see this in future examples.

00:09:51.750 --> 00:09:54.280
So here, another new
suggestion for an action title.

00:09:54.280 --> 00:09:55.470
Again, pause the video.

00:09:55.470 --> 00:09:57.690
Is this a good action title or not?

00:09:57.690 --> 00:10:00.900
Expansion to North
America and Asia Pacific

00:10:00.900 --> 00:10:02.873
creates a positive EBIT potential.

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:07.640
And what you see here, is that this is now

00:10:07.640 --> 00:10:11.200
much more concrete than the
first one and the second one,

00:10:11.200 --> 00:10:14.410
because now it talks
about the specific regions

00:10:14.410 --> 00:10:16.490
that this page is looking into.

00:10:16.490 --> 00:10:18.312
So yes, now we're really getting closer

00:10:18.312 --> 00:10:21.080
to a good result, to a good action title.

00:10:21.080 --> 00:10:23.480
And nevertheless, I would argue

00:10:23.480 --> 00:10:25.300
that you can do better than that.

00:10:25.300 --> 00:10:28.010
Because when possible,
it's always a good idea

00:10:28.010 --> 00:10:32.220
to really quantify the
things that you analyzed.

00:10:32.220 --> 00:10:35.670
And now, this is what the
next example is all about.

00:10:35.670 --> 00:10:38.540
And here again, expansion to
North America and Asia Pacific

00:10:38.540 --> 00:10:43.540
creates a positive EBIT
potential of 22 euro million.

00:10:47.720 --> 00:10:49.810
So, I mean what's wrong with that?

00:10:49.810 --> 00:10:52.020
So this is, I would
say, already very good.

00:10:52.020 --> 00:10:54.270
And if you catch that, so 22 million

00:10:54.270 --> 00:10:57.390
would be the sum of the 12
million and the 10 million here.

00:10:57.390 --> 00:10:59.800
Or, it says also here the 22 million.

00:10:59.800 --> 00:11:01.840
The only thing that I would
criticize with this title

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:04.370
is that it is a bit too wordy.

00:11:04.370 --> 00:11:08.290
You can formulate the very
same message with fewer words,

00:11:08.290 --> 00:11:11.440
and this is usually always
advantageous, because then

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:14.780
the reader doesn't have
to go into too much detail

00:11:14.780 --> 00:11:16.837
to really get the key message out of it.

00:11:18.400 --> 00:11:20.110
So, one final suggestion.

00:11:20.110 --> 00:11:23.010
Expansion to North
America and Asia Pacific

00:11:23.010 --> 00:11:25.243
with 22 euro million EBIT potential.

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:29.310
And I would argue yes, this
is a good action title.

00:11:29.310 --> 00:11:32.080
It summarizes the key message of the page.

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:33.863
It is pretty concise and short.

00:11:34.740 --> 00:11:38.800
It doesn't use too much words
to put this message across.

00:11:38.800 --> 00:11:40.950
So I think this would
be a feasible option.

00:11:42.080 --> 00:11:43.720
And of course, in the end,
I think it's important

00:11:43.720 --> 00:11:45.970
to emphasize that of
course, there's nothing like

00:11:45.970 --> 00:11:50.260
the mathematically correct
perfect action title.

00:11:50.260 --> 00:11:52.160
There are many feasible options,

00:11:52.160 --> 00:11:55.840
but probably some action
titles are better than others.

00:11:55.840 --> 00:11:58.810
And I would just really
encourage you to think about

00:11:58.810 --> 00:12:01.780
whether your action title
is as good as it could be,

00:12:01.780 --> 00:12:05.810
and I hope that this example
gives you some food for thought

00:12:05.810 --> 00:12:08.290
in order to get to that conclusion.

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:11.380
So just in the end, what
I would like you to do is,

00:12:11.380 --> 00:12:14.190
again here in the Q&amp;A
section of this course

00:12:14.190 --> 00:12:16.360
that appears in the bottom of the page

00:12:16.360 --> 00:12:17.880
if you hover here with the mouse,

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:21.090
I think it says "Browse Q&amp;A", just enter

00:12:21.090 --> 00:12:23.690
maybe an alternative solution
that you came up with,

00:12:23.690 --> 00:12:25.573
and then you have the
opportunity to also check out

00:12:25.573 --> 00:12:28.910
what other classmates
of yours came up with,

00:12:28.910 --> 00:12:30.710
and then hopefully you can also learn

00:12:30.710 --> 00:12:34.303
from these other solutions
that other people created.

00:12:35.590 --> 00:12:37.810
So guys, I hope you enjoyed this course

00:12:37.810 --> 00:12:40.150
on creating good and
compelling action titles.

00:12:40.150 --> 00:12:42.400
Maybe you even had a coffee just as I had,

